.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
installs, upgrades, removes, and inspects
.Xr mport 5
packages.
It can work with repository packages, local package files, and the local
package database.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following global options are supported by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width ".Fl o Ar output-path"
.It Cm --allow-old-release
Install package files that were built for a MidnightBSD release other than
the target release.
Package files record the release they were built on, and
.Cm add ,
.Cm install
and
.Cm update
refuse one whose release differs from the target, because libraries from
another release may carry different symbols or shared library versions.
The target release is the one named by
.Ev ABI_FILE
when set, then the
.Cm target_os
setting, otherwise the running system.
Use this option, or set
.Ev MPORT_ALLOW_OLD_RELEASE ,
to install such a file anyway, for example software that is no longer
available for the current release or packages for a jail running an older
release.
The option applies to the named package and to any dependencies installed
with it.
.It Fl b, Cm --brief
Use brief output when supported by the command.
.It Fl c Ar chroot-path , Cm --chroot Ar chroot-path
Run inside the specified chroot.
.It Fl f, Cm --force
Force the operation when supported.
This currently applies to commands such as
.Cm add ,
.Cm install
and
.Cm delete .
For
.Cm add
and
.Cm install ,
the package named on the command line is reinstalled even when the same
version is already installed, and registry rows left behind by a failed
install are cleared first.
The flag applies only to the named package; its dependencies are never
reinstalled because of it.
.It Fl o Ar output-path , Cm --output Ar output-path
Write downloaded package files to
.Ar output-path .
.It Fl q, Cm --quiet
Reduce output verbosity and suppress download progress.
.It Fl U, Cm --no-index
Skip automatic index updates for this invocation.
.It Fl V, Cm --verbose
Increase output verbosity.
.It Fl v, Cm --version
Display the current version of
.Nm
and exit.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
The following commands are supported by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width ".Cm annotate Fl A Ar package Ar tag Ar value"
.It Cm add Oo Fl A Oc Oo Fl l Oc Ar package-file ...
Install one or more local
.Pa .mport
package files.
If
.Fl A
is specified, mark the installed package as automatic.
If the package is already installed and the local package file contains a newer
version,
.Nm
updates it by removing the installed package and installing the local file.
.Pp
Dependencies that are not installed, or are installed for a previous
release of MidnightBSD, are looked for as package files in the same directory
and installed first.
Dependencies that are already installed for the running release are left
alone, and
.Fl f
never applies to them.
A dependency installed for a previous release is also left alone when it
provides no shared libraries, since nothing links against it, or when every
shared library it provides is also provided by a package built for the
running release, since the run-time linker finds the current copy; see
.Xr mport.create 1 .
.Pp
After the dependency check, a warning names each shared library the package
needs that no installed package provides and the base system does not ship.
It is a warning rather than a refusal because packages registered before
shared libraries were recorded have no provided list.
With
.Fl l ,
only the named package files are installed and no dependency package files
are looked for; a missing dependency is then an error.
This matches the behaviour of
.Xr mport.install 1 ,
which the ports collection uses to install packages it has just built.
.Pp
.Cm add
was written for installing packages from the install media.
For repository installs, use
.Cm install .
.It Cm annotate Op Fl a Op Fl q Fl S Ar package Ar tag
Show the value of an annotation tag for a package.
With
.Fl a ,
show the tag for all installed packages.
With
.Fl q ,
use abbreviated output suitable for scripts.
.It Cm annotate Op Fl a Op Fl q Fl A Ar package Ar tag Ar value
Add an annotation tag to a package.
.It Cm annotate Fl D Ar package Ar tag
Delete an annotation tag from a package.
.It Cm audit Op Fl r Op Ar package
Display vulnerable installed packages using CPE data matched against the
MidnightBSD security feed.
With
.Fl r ,
also include packages that depend on a vulnerable package.
If
.Ar package
is specified, audit only that package.
.It Cm autoremove
Remove packages that were installed automatically and are no longer required
by any explicitly installed package.
.It Cm clean
Remove package files no longer present in the index and perform maintenance on
the local package database.
.It Cm config list
List all available configuration settings.
.It Cm config get Ar setting
Display the value of
.Ar setting .
.It Cm config set Ar setting Ar value
Set
.Ar setting
to
.Ar value .
.It Cm cpe Op Ar package ...
List Common Platform Enumeration identifiers for installed packages.
If one or more package names are specified, restrict output to those packages.
.It Cm delete Ar package ...
Remove one or more installed packages.
.It Cm deleteall
Remove all installed packages.
This is primarily useful for testing or major operating system upgrades.
.It Cm download Op Fl a Op Fl d Op Ar package ...
Download package files without installing them.
With
.Fl a ,
download all available packages.
With
.Fl d ,
also download dependencies.
.It Cm export Ar file
Export package metadata or a package list to
.Ar file .
.It Cm import Ar file
Import package metadata or a package list from
.Ar file .
.It Cm index
Refresh the package index immediately instead of waiting for the automatic
update interval.
.It Cm info Oo Fl e Oc Oo Fl b Oc Oo Fl B Oc Ar package
Display detailed information about an installed package or an indexed package.
With
.Fl e ,
exit with status 0 if the package is installed and 1 otherwise, printing
nothing.
With
.Fl b ,
list the shared libraries the installed package provides; with
.Fl B ,
the shared libraries it requires.
Both lists are recorded when the package is built; see
.Xr mport.create 1 .
A package built before that was recorded has empty lists.
.It Cm install Op Fl A Op Fl M Op Fl y Ar package ...
Fetch and install one or more packages from the configured repository.
With
.Fl A ,
mark the installed packages as automatic.
With
.Fl M ,
ignore missing dependencies and attempt the installation anyway.
With
.Fl y ,
assume yes for confirmation prompts.
If a requested package is not available in the package index and a populated
.Pa /usr/mports
tree is present,
.Nm
prints guidance for installing a matching port or searching the ports tree.
.It Cm list Op Cm updates | Cm up | Cm prime
Without arguments, list installed packages.
The
.Cm updates
or
.Cm up
subcommand lists installed packages with updates available.
The
.Cm prime
subcommand lists packages installed explicitly rather than as dependencies.
.It Cm lock Ar package
Prevent a package from being modified by upgrade or delete operations.
.It Cm locks
List all locked packages.
.It Cm mirror list
List available package mirrors.
.It Cm mirror select
Ping known mirrors, select the closest responding mirror, and save it as the
default.
.It Cm purl Op Ar package ...
List Package URL values for installed packages.
If one or more package names are specified, restrict output to those packages.
.It Cm query Op Fl aCgix Op Fl e Ar expression Ar format Op Ar pattern ...
Print installed package metadata using a
.Fx
.Nm pkg
.Cm query Ns -style
format string.
With no
.Ar pattern
arguments, all installed packages are selected.
With one or more patterns, package names are matched exactly unless a matching
mode option is specified.
.Pp
The following options are supported:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fl e Ar expression"
.It Fl a
Select all installed packages explicitly.
.It Fl C
Use case-sensitive matching.
.It Fl e Ar expression
Filter matched packages with a scalar expression.
The expression language supports field truth checks, equality and inequality,
glob matching with
.Ql ~ ,
version comparisons with
.Ql < ,
.Ql <= ,
.Ql > ,
and
.Ql >= ,
and boolean
.Ql && ,
.Ql || ,
and leading
.Ql ! .
.It Fl g
Treat patterns as shell glob patterns.
.It Fl i
Use case-insensitive matching.
.It Fl x
Treat patterns as extended regular expressions.
.El
.Pp
The
.Ar format
string supports percent fields including
.Ql \&%n
for package name,
.Ql \&%v
for version,
.Ql \&%o
for origin,
.Ql \&%p
for prefix,
.Ql \&%m
for maintainer annotation,
.Ql \&%c
for comment,
.Ql \&%e
for description,
.Ql \&%w
for WWW annotation,
.Ql \&%a
for automatic install flag,
.Ql \&%k
for locked flag,
.Ql \&%t
for install timestamp,
.Ql \&%s
or
.Ql \&%sb
for flat size in bytes,
.Ql \&%sh
or
.Ql \&%h
for human-readable flat size,
.Ql \&%M
for package message,
.Ql \&%X
for index hash,
.Ql \&%l
for license metadata,
.Ql \&%q
for target architecture, and
.Ql \&%P
for package URL.
.Pp
List fields are printed comma-separated:
.Ql \&%A
annotations,
.Ql \&%C
categories,
.Ql \&%D
directories,
.Ql \&%F
files,
.Ql \&%L
licenses,
.Ql \&%O
options,
.Ql \&%d
dependencies, and
.Ql \&%r
reverse dependencies.
.Ql \&%#X
prints the count for a supported list field
.Ql \&%X ,
and
.Ql \&%?X
prints
.Ql 1
when the list is present or
.Ql 0
when it is empty.
.Pp
The
.Fx
.Nm pkg
.Cm query
.Fl F
package-file mode is not supported by
.Nm
in this version.
.It Cm search Ar query ...
Search package names and descriptions.
Glob patterns such as
.Dq *php*
are supported.
.It Cm shell
Start a
.Xr sqlite3 1
session connected to the
.Nm
master package database.
.It Cm stats
Display statistics about available and installed packages.
.It Cm unlock Ar package
Remove a package lock.
.It Cm update Ar package ...
Update one or more installed packages.
Wildcard arguments are supported.
When an installed Python, PHP, or version-prefixed Ruby package uses an older
repository default,
.Nm
offers to switch it to the package built for the current default.
If both versions remain available, the old version may instead be retained.
.It Cm upgrade
Upgrade all installed packages to the newest available versions.
Packages that are still registered for an older MidnightBSD release are
updated first, lowest-level dependencies before the packages that use them,
so that nothing is upgraded against libraries from the previous release.
A package that links against a shared library another package provides is
ordered after that package whether or not the port declared the dependency.
A package from an older release for which the repository has no package is
reported and left in place.
The remaining packages are then upgraded in dependency order.
.It Cm verify Oo Fl d Oc Oo Fl r Oc Op Ar package ...
Verify that installed package files have not been deleted or modified.
If package names are provided, verify only those packages.
With
.Fl d ,
report installed packages whose recorded dependencies are not installed,
and recorded shared library requirements that no installed package provides
and the base system does not ship.
With
.Fl r ,
recompute and store checksums for the named packages.
This is useful after intentional local modifications.
.It Cm version Oo Fl I | Fl P Ar ports-dir Oc Oo Fl l Ar status Oc Oo Fl L Ar status Oc Op Ar package ...
Compare each installed package, or only the named
.Ar package
arguments, with the newest version the package index offers and print the
package name and version followed by a status character:
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Ql <
the installed version is older
.It Ql =
the versions are equal
.It Ql >
the installed version is newer
.It Ql \&?
nothing to compare with: the package is not in the index or ports tree
.It Ql \&!
the comparison failed
.El
.Pp
A package found in the index only by its origin, under another name,
is reported as
.Ql < .
With
.Fl P ,
or when
.Ev PORTSDIR
is set, compare with the ports tree in
.Ar ports-dir
instead of the index, using the version
.Xr make 1
computes for
.Va PKGVERSION
in the directory named by each package's origin, with its flavor.
This runs
.Xr make 1
once per package, so naming packages is much faster than checking all of
them on a large tree.
The index is not loaded or fetched in this mode.
.Fl I
compares with the index even when
.Ev PORTSDIR
is set.
.Fl l
shows only packages with the given status and
.Fl L
hides them.
With
.Fl q ,
print only the package names and versions;
with
.Fl V ,
also print the version compared with.
.It Cm version Fl t Ar version1 Ar version2
Compare two version strings and print
.Ql <
if
.Ar version1
is older,
.Ql =
if they are equal, or
.Ql >
if
.Ar version1
is newer.
.It Cm shlib Oo Fl q Oc Oo Fl P | Fl R Oc Ar library
Show which installed packages provide
.Ar library
and which require it, by the shared library records made when each package
was built.
.Ar library
is a soname such as
.Dq libfoo.so.1 ,
optionally with a path, which is ignored, and optionally with the
.Dq :32
or
.Dq :Linux
suffix used for compatibility objects.
With
.Fl P ,
show only providers; with
.Fl R ,
only packages that require it.
With
.Fl q ,
print only package names and versions.
A library the base system ships is reported as such when nothing provides
it.
.It Cm which Op Fl q Op Fl o Ar path
Show which installed package owns
.Ar path .
With
.Fl q ,
print only the package name and version.
With
.Fl o ,
print the package origin instead.
.El
.Sh SETTINGS
The following configuration settings commonly affect
.Nm
behavior:
.Bl -tag -width ".Cm index_autoupdate"
.It Cm mirror_region
Select the mirror region used for downloads.
Valid values currently include
.Dq us ,
.Dq us2 ,
.Dq us3 ,
.Dq uk ,
and
.Dq jp .
The current list is stored in the
.Pa mirrors
table of
.Pa /var/db/mport/index.db .
.It Cm target_os
Override the operating system version used when fetching and installing
packages.
.Ev ABI_FILE ,
when set, takes precedence.
If neither is set,
.Nm
checks
.Pa /bin/midnightbsd-version
first and falls back to the running kernel version.
.It Cm index_last_check
Timestamp of the last index update check.
.It Cm index_autoupdate
Enable or disable automatic index refresh.
If set to
.Dq NO
or
.Dq FALSE ,
automatic updates are skipped unless the index is missing.
This is the persistent equivalent of the global
.Fl U
flag.
.It Cm handle_rc_scripts
If set to
.Dq yes
or
.Dq true ,
run rc.d start and stop scripts shipped by packages.
If set to
.Dq no
or
.Dq false ,
do not run them.
.El
.Pp
Use
.Cm mport config list
to see additional settings supported by the local installation.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev MPORT_ALLOW_OLD_RELEASE"
.It Ev ABI_FILE
Path to a binary built for the target system, such as
.Pa /bin/sh
in a cross-build sysroot or a jail.
When set to a non-empty value, the target release is read from the
MidnightBSD ABI note in that file instead of from the
.Cm target_os
setting or the running system, and is used everywhere the release matters:
fetching the index and packages, installing, upgrading and creating
packages.
A file without a MidnightBSD ABI note, such as a Linux binary, leaves the
release to
.Cm target_os
and the running system.
A file that cannot be read or is not an ELF object is an error.
.It Ev ASSUME_ALWAYS_YES
If set to a non-empty value, answer yes to confirmation prompts.
.It Ev MPORT_ALLOW_OLD_RELEASE
If set to a non-empty value, behave as if
.Cm --allow-old-release
had been given.
This is read by the library, so it also applies to
.Xr mport.install 1 .
.It Ev FETCH_BIND_ADDRESS
Bind outgoing network connections to the specified hostname or IP address.
.It Ev FTP_LOGIN
Default FTP login if none was provided in the URL.
.It Ev FTP_PASSIVE_MODE
If set to
.Ql no ,
forces the FTP code to use active mode.
If set to any other value, forces passive mode even if the application
requested active mode.
.It Ev FTP_PASSWORD
Default FTP password if the remote server requests one and none was
provided in the URL.
.It Ev FTP_PROXY
URL of the proxy to use for FTP requests.
If no scheme is specified,
.Dq ftp
is assumed.
.It Ev MPORT_FORCE_HTTP
If set to a non-empty value, fetch package indexes and package bundles over
HTTP by rewriting HTTPS download URLs to HTTP.
.It Ev HANDLE_RC_SCRIPTS
If set to a non-empty value, start or stop rc.d scripts included with the
package.
.It Ev PORTSDIR
Location of a ports tree.
If set to a non-empty value,
.Cm version
compares installed packages with that tree rather than the package index.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Search for a package:
.Dl $ mport search curl
.Pp
Install a package from the repository:
.Dl # mport install curl
.Pp
Install a package without refreshing the index:
.Dl # mport -U install curl
.Pp
Install a local package file:
.Dl # mport add /home/myuser/mypkg.mport
.Pp
List installed packages:
.Dl $ mport list
.Pp
List packages needing upgrades:
.Dl $ mport list updates
.Pp
Show detailed package information:
.Dl $ mport info gmake
.Pp
Print installed package names and versions:
.Dl $ mport query '%n-%v'
.Pp
Print the origin and size for installed packages matching a glob:
.Dl $ mport query -g '%o %sh' 'gma*'
.Pp
Determine which package installed a file:
.Dl $ mport which /usr/local/bin/curl
.Pp
Lock a package before a system upgrade:
.Dl # mport lock curl
.Pp
Upgrade all installed packages:
.Dl # mport upgrade
.Pp
Upgrade a single package:
.Dl # mport update gmake
.Pp
Remove unneeded dependencies:
.Dl # mport autoremove
.Pp
Check installed packages for checksum mismatches:
.Dl # mport verify
.Pp
Search for all XFCE-related packages:
.Dl $ mport search xfce*
